From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:29:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: make pre-cal MCU command synchronous

Group and DPD pre-calibration is pushed to the firmware in a
tight loop of 1 KiB chunks. With the final send fire-and-forget
the driver can outrun the MCU and the upload lands wrong or wedges
the firmware; wait for each chunk to be acknowledged. Add a
dev_dbg per chunk for tracing. Same fix as the mt7996 counterpart.

Fixes: OWRT-9347

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -3088,7 +3088,7 @@ static int mt7915_mcu_set_pre_cal(struct
 	skb_put_data(skb, &req, sizeof(req));
 	skb_put_data(skb, data, len);
 
-	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb, cmd, false);
+	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb, cmd, true);
 }
 
 int mt7915_mcu_apply_group_cal(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
@@ -3109,6 +3109,9 @@ int mt7915_mcu_apply_group_cal(struct mt
 
 		len = min_t(u32, total, MT_EE_CAL_UNIT);
 
+		dev_dbg(dev->mt76.dev, "apply pre-cal idx=%u cal[0]=0x%02x len=%d total=%d\n",
+				idx, ((unsigned char *)cal)[0], len, total);
+
 		ret = mt7915_mcu_set_pre_cal(dev, idx, cal, len,
 					     MCU_EXT_CMD(GROUP_PRE_CAL_INFO));
 		if (ret)
